*======================================================================
* resident.a99 - code assembled INTO THE KERNEL's pages, so every module can
* BL to it directly (app.json "resident").  Two small routines to show what
* that gives that MODCALL does not, and the line editor from lib/ so that it
* is carried once for both modules.
*======================================================================

* RSUM - R0 = the address of a table of words, R1 = how many: R0 = their sum.
* The table may be in the CALLER's code (slot C): the caller is mapped while
* this runs.  Uses R1, R2.
RSUM   CLR  R2
RSU1   A    *R0+,R2
       DEC  R1
       JNE  RSU1
       MOV  R2,R0
       RT

* RCALL - call the routine at R1 once for each R0 = 0 to R2-1 and add up what
* it answers in R0: R0 = the sum.  The routine is in the caller's module, so
* it can only be called because the caller's module is still mapped.  It may
* change R0-R5.  Uses R6-R9.
RCALL  .enter
       MOV  R1,R9
       MOV  R2,R8
       CLR  R7
       CLR  R6
RCL1   C    R7,R8
       JHE  RCL2
       MOV  R7,R0
       BL   *R9
       A    R0,R6
       INC  R7
       JMP  RCL1
RCL2   MOV  R6,R0
       .leave
       RT

       COPY "linein.a99"
